  "A 74-year-old woman has very high-risk myelodysplastic syndrome with elevated blasts that remain below the leukemia threshold. Which outcome is she at greatest risk of within 5 years?",
  [["Progression to acute myeloid leukemia",
    "Correct. Very high-risk myelodysplastic syndrome has a median overall survival of 9 months and more than an 80% risk of developing acute myeloid leukemia within 5 years."],
   ["Progression to polycythemia vera",
    "Polycythemia vera is a myeloproliferative neoplasm of red cell overproduction; myelodysplasia gives cytopenias and progresses to acute leukemia. Tell: high-risk myelodysplasia heads toward acute myeloid leukemia.", "competing diagnosis"],
   ["Progression to lymphoblastic leukemia",
    "Myelodysplastic syndrome is a myeloid malignancy, so its progression is to acute myeloid leukemia, not to a lymphoid leukemia. Tell: myeloid disease progresses to a myeloid leukemia.", "confused mechanism or drug class"],
   ["Spontaneous recovery of counts",
    "Very high-risk disease has a median overall survival of 9 months; counts do not spontaneously recover. Tell: the expected course is progression to acute myeloid leukemia.", "reversed direction or value"]],
